{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnSu1SfAxQbdGTN9Jqgg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm looking at whether the base model's copy scores line up with how much each head strengthens, and they don't. The base model has very clean copy heads and anti-copy heads, with the strongest suppressors at L7h1, L8h0, L9h1, L11h3 and L15h1.\n\nI'm now weighing the remaining copy-head candidates (L9h2, L11h1, L15h0, L15h2, L15h3, L17h1, L3h2) against the strengthening numbers, which are around 0.1% and too noisy to trust on their own. Since the per-head evidence points in conflicting directions, I'm considering whether the aggregate sign-through-copy argument holds up.\n\nI'm checking whether the full-space OV identity result holds up by splitting it into its O and V parts, and I'm also wondering whether the MLP has a similar identity-like structure that could carry the sign difference.\n\nI'm weighing whether the OV eigenvalue result fits a copying story, since that's the standard way to read it. I also want to check the T-seeking signal in L15 and L16, because it points the other way, though it may just reflect attention to answer-type tokens in general rather than the answer position.\n\nI'm now checking whether the answer-position query feature shows up in the rank-1 Δq at L12, which has a shared input direction across heads. Next I'd map each head's key-side direction back through W_K and compare it to the token embedding metric, then see whether the value directions line up across layers.\n\nI'm checking whether the O and V parts of the OV identity hold up separately, and whether the MLP might carry a similar identity-like structure. Then I'll look at which earlier components write the value direction v.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17433,"cache_read_input_tokens":133463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17433},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"0ffb7465-72c1-45e9-8131-6a1520d13e7b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:16:30.945Z","request_id":"req_011CgnSu12rnUTzCkWZA21id","thinking_duration_ms":16583,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnSu1SfAxQbdGTN9Jqgg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run 21 showed no relationship between a head's base copying score and its relative up-weighting in A vs B (Pearson −0.09, Spearman −0.05, null sd 0.12; T-metric +0.00). Relative per-head strengthening is about 0.1% and noise-dominated, so this test is null. It does map the base circuitry, which is useful for describing roles:\n- Clean copy heads (score ≈ +0.9 to +1.0): L3h2, L7h0, L7h2, L7h3, L8h2, L9h2, L10h0, L11h1, L12h2, L13h2, L14h1, L15h0, L15h2, L15h3 and L17h1.\n- Clean copy-suppression heads (≈ −0.9 to −1.0): L7h1, L8h0, L9h1, L11h3 and L15h1.\n\np(A) ≈ 0.55.\n\nThe most structured A−B changes are in the query projections: rank-1 components far above the background in L12, L5, L10, L9, L1 and L6. If the behavioural difference is \"attend to the user's guess or not\", these query changes are where it lives. Their input direction v should be a feature present at the position where the answer is produced. Their key-side target (Δq's head-space output pushed through W_K) tells what kind of token is attended. So for the top Δq component of each layer I'll compute:\n1. the input directions v across layers and their mutual cosines (is it one persistent query feature?);\n2. the key-residual direction each head's Δq targets, using k_norm and RoPE-averaged weighting, and its overlap with the answer-token subspace T;\n3. the spread of the change over heads.\n\nThis is symmetric so far, but it pins down what the query changes are about.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\nP=lambda L:f\"model.layers.{L}.\"\nT=np.load(\"/work/T5mlp.npy\")\nlt=A.config[\"layer_types\"]; hd=256\nV={}; KT={}\nfor L in range(18):\n    p=P(L)\n    Di=1+A.get(p+\"input_layernorm.weight\")\n    dq=A.get(p+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")-B.get(p+\"self_attn.q_proj.weight\")\n    U,s,Vt=np.linalg.svd(dq,full_matrices=False)\n    v=Vt[0]*Di; V[L]=v/np.linalg.norm(v)\n    theta=1e6 if lt[L]==\"full_attention\" else 1e4\n    f=theta**(-np.arange(128)/128.0); wp=np.cos(np.outer(f,np.arange(1,61))).mean(1); w=np.concatenate([wp,wp])\n    kn=1+A.get(p+\"self_attn.k_norm.weight\"); qn=1+A.get(p+\"self_attn.q_norm.weight\")\n    Wk=(A.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\")+B.get(p+\"self_attn.k_proj.weight\"))/2\n    out=[]\n    for h in range(4):\n        uh=U[h*hd:(h+1)*hd,0]*s[0]*qn\n        kdir=Di*(Wk.T@(kn*w*uh))       # key-residual (embedding-metric) direction targeted\n        n=np.linalg.norm(kdir)\n        tfrac=np.linalg.norm(T.T@kdir)/n if n>0 else 0\n        out.append((np.linalg.norm(U[h*hd:(h+1)*hd,0])**2, tfrac))\n    vT=np.linalg.norm(T.T@V[L])\n    print(f\"L{L:2d} s0/med={s[0]/np.median(s):5.1f}  v.T-frac={vT:.3f}  per-head (mass, key-dir T-frac): \"+\" \".join(f\"({m:.2f},{t:.3f})\" for m,t in out))\nprint(\"random T-frac ~\", np.sqrt(5/640).round(3))\nLsel=[1,5,6,7,9,10,12,13,15,17]\nM=np.array([[abs(V[a]@V[b]) for b in Lsel] for a in Lsel])\nprint(\"cos between top-dq input dirs across layers\", Lsel); print(M.round(2))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17433,"cache_read_input_tokens":133463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17433},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9fb2689-71d1-4789-9324-4ca53bd1b486","uuid":"79f6f82d-041c-4b18-9204-90d32c6bf7b6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T22:16:41.273Z","request_id":"req_011CgnSu12rnUTzCkWZA21id"}
